1
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,000
The police are onto us.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,590
We can't go through with the deal tonight.

3
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:05,960
Police!

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,160
Hello, Officer Mok.

5
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:10,030
I'm Joseph.

6
00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:11,000
I'm eager to learn.

7
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,320
So what do you think To Si Hong is doing here?

8
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,350
This is very likely an underground casino.

9
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:16,710
It's not surprising that he

10
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:17,550
came here to scam people.

11
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,320
Watch out!

12
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:25,070
I suspect the casino owner was trying to silence him.

13
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:26,280
That guy said he'd just

14
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,550
bought the bike and brought it in for modifications.

15
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:30,510
But I could tell straight away it wasn't legit.

16
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:32,670
Go check the stolen-vehicle records.

17
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,350
Bye-bye.

18
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:33,880
But...

19
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:35,070
Get to it.

20
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,280
Don't hold me up. I'm meeting someone.

21
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:39,070
Yes, sir.

22
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:14,700
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

23
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:17,900
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

24
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:20,810
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

25
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:23,240
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

26
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:26,220
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

27
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:30,380
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

28
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:35,170
♪I'm willing to wait♪

29
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:38,860
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

30
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,660
♪I want to share my life with you♪

31
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:48,080
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

32
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:50,230
♪In this cold and gray city♪

33
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:51,940
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

34
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:54,390
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

35
00:01:54,470 --> 00:01:55,050
♪Stay with me♪

36
00:01:55,190 --> 00:01:57,800
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

37
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:58,580
♪Stay with me♪

38
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,500
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

39
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:04,000
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

40
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:07,040
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

41
00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:10,080
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

42
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:14,300
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

43
00:02:16,150 --> 00:02:18,180
[Ash]
[Episode 5]

44
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,030
What do you think?

45
00:02:57,430 --> 00:03:01,120
So this is the view you get while you work?

46
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,120
I spend more time dealing

47
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,430
with clients and paperwork.

48
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,750
This view is mostly for clients.

49
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:11,560
Hey.

50
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,910
Have all your employees left?

51
00:04:14,870 --> 00:04:15,960
I don't know.

52
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,920
No touching.

53
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:37,720
Sorry, Officer.

54
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,040
Is that an order?

55
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:47,120
Mr. Hui,

56
00:04:48,270 --> 00:04:50,000
do as I say.

57
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,120
Step back.

58
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,390
Undress.

59
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:40,950
Freeze.

60
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,830
Keep going.

61
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,670
Your birthday is coming up.

62
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:54,390
How about we go on a glacier trip?

63
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,550
If I'm staying at a hotel with you,

64
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,390
do we really have time for sightseeing?

65
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,000
I can book a hotel room

66
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,750
with a view of the glaciers.

67
00:09:17,670 --> 00:09:21,240
Police officers can't just take leave whenever they want.

68
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,550
How about you watch a film with me instead?

69
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,000
Sure.

70
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,360
I'll book a private screening.

71
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,240
What film do you want to watch?

72
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,240
No need for that.

73
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:34,200
Can we just go to the cinema

74
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,720
like everyone else?

75
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:38,960
Sure.

76
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:39,750
Okay.

77
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:06,480
Foon Gor.

78
00:11:09,030 --> 00:11:10,200
Foon Gor?

79
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:14,960
Foon Gor.

80
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:16,720
Huh?

81
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:17,870
Shawn?

82
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,360
You're here to eat?

83
00:11:19,390 --> 00:11:20,200
No.

84
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,910
I came here specifically to see you.

85
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:23,080
Huh?

86
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,000
What's the matter?

87
00:11:24,550 --> 00:11:25,960
Your birthday is coming up.

88
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,320
I booked a set menu at a three-Michelin-star restaurant.

89
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,960
I want to take you there.

90
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,080
Sorry.

91
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:37,360
I've already made plans that night.

92
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:38,840
Maybe next time.

93
00:11:39,550 --> 00:11:40,960
And you don't need to spend so much.

94
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:44,200
Who are you meeting?

95
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:47,750
A friend.

96
00:11:49,030 --> 00:11:49,840
A friend?

97
00:12:01,670 --> 00:12:03,240
You're meeting Hui Loek To?

98
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:06,750
Why do you ask?

99
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,750
His family background is complicated.

100
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:14,550
I don't think he's a good person.

101
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,150
Don't worry.

102
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:18,000
I'm a good judge of character.

103
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,080
I know how to handle my own affairs.

104
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:22,200
Come on.

105
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,120
What do you want to eat this time?

106
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:23,600
It's on me.

107
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:25,030
Excuse me.

108
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:26,150
Coming.

109
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,240
I'll have another buttered pineapple bun.

110
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,320
A buttered pineapple bun.

111
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,000
Yes.

112
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,670
And one more...

113
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,150
Mr. Hui.

114
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,720
Ms. So is ready to see you now.

115
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:54,550
All right.

116
00:12:55,390 --> 00:12:56,080
This way.

117
00:13:13,390 --> 00:13:14,550
Thank you, Lalin.

118
00:13:14,550 --> 00:13:16,390
It's a pleasure to be working with you.

119
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:18,080
The pleasure is mine.

120
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,840
Ms. So.

121
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,240
Hi, Vincent.

122
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,440
You just secured another client.

123
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,750
Congratulations.

124
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:40,200
Lunch is on me.

125
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,120
My treat.

126
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:43,320
You must be joking, Vincent.

127
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,960
This deal is nothing compared to yours.

128
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:49,840
Don't be so modest. If the So family didn't have the financial strength,

129
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,240
I wouldn't have chosen to work with you.

130
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,030
So? Do you have any news to share with me?

131
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,750
I arranged this lunch with you today

132
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:58,510
because I wanted to talk to you.

133
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,600
I discussed the project you proposed last time

134
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,960
with my dad.

135
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:03,720
I'm sorry,

136
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,360
but I don't think we can take part this time.

137
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,200
I can probably guess why.

138
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:12,000
I know the So family was going to invest a substantial amount this time.

139
00:14:12,390 --> 00:14:15,200
And you wanted a seat on Tin Ping Group's board.

140
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,240
I'd already agreed to that.

141
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Didn't you always want to enter the property industry?

142
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:21,550
Have you made up your mind already?

143
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,510
If you're unhappy with the terms,

144
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:24,840
we can still discuss them.

145
00:14:25,750 --> 00:14:27,510
I underestimated how risk-averse my father was.

146
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:30,000
He doesn't want to invest in other industries.

147
00:14:30,670 --> 00:14:32,440
I tried my best to persuade him.

148
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,030
But he said unless someone from Tin Ping became part of our family,

149
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,840
he wouldn't use the group's funds

150
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:39,120
to invest in Tin Ping.

151
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:40,750
I see.

152
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:44,750
But if the So family only does business with relatives,

153
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:46,910
it'll be difficult for the business to grow.

154
00:14:47,750 --> 00:14:49,510
I think he was just putting pressure on me.

155
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:51,600
Last time, I casually asked how he'd react

156
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:55,390
if I brought home a capable woman instead of a capable man.

157
00:14:55,550 --> 00:14:57,030
He nearly had a heart attack.

158
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,030
So whenever he gets the chance, he pushes me to get married.

159
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,510
I have a way

160
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:12,320
to get our two groups to work together.

161
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,120
Would you like to hear it?

162
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:24,440
Let's sit for a while.

163
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:25,510
Okay.

164
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,000
I haven't had a moment this peaceful in a long time.

165
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:42,550
I bet.

166
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,150
You're always so busy

167
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:48,120
and have to manage things on both sides of the law.

168
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,600
How could you possibly have time to sit by the sea?

169
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,150
I don't care if you like hearing it.

170
00:15:56,270 --> 00:15:57,440
I'm only stating the facts.

171
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,200
Don't worry.

172
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:06,120
I'll clean up Sheng Tung

173
00:16:07,030 --> 00:16:09,750
and completely distance my brother and myself from the gangs.

174
00:16:11,550 --> 00:16:12,630
I hope so.

175
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:21,550
Look over there.

176
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,360
This is for you.

177
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,200
Why are you suddenly giving me a watch?

178
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,200
Well,

179
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,390
you handcuffed me once.

180
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,720
This time, I'm handcuffing you back.

181
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:55,720
So you mean you want to tie me down?

182
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:02,200
No.

183
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:09,960
I mean from now on, every minute and every second of your life belongs to me.

184
00:17:11,350 --> 00:17:14,070
When did you learn to say such cheesy lines?

185
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,240
Still, I'll give you credit for that.

186
00:17:19,750 --> 00:17:20,960
Is it really that cheesy?

187
00:17:21,350 --> 00:17:22,550
Do I get a reward?

188
00:17:24,550 --> 00:17:25,350
Come here.

189
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,070
I'll tell you.

190
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:32,310
That's it?

191
00:17:34,070 --> 00:17:35,550
Isn't that enough?

192
00:19:39,590 --> 00:19:40,350
We made it in time.

193
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,240
The film hasn't started.

194
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,000
Let's take a photo together.

195
00:20:12,830 --> 00:20:15,030
Why are you suddenly in the mood to take photos today?

196
00:20:15,550 --> 00:20:17,000
It's my first time going out with you.

197
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,830
And it's your birthday.

198
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:21,160
We should leave something to remember it by.

199
00:20:23,550 --> 00:20:25,440
Since when have you cared about making memories?

200
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,350
As long as it makes you happy,

201
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:32,110
I'll do anything.

202
00:20:41,550 --> 00:20:42,350
What is it?

203
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,110
You look

204
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:45,510
especially cute today.

205
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:48,200
Give me the tickets.

206
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,410
[Palace Theatre]

207
00:21:01,110 --> 00:21:02,400
I'll keep mine safe

208
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,350
as a memento of today.

209
00:21:06,590 --> 00:21:07,960
You keep yours safe too.

210
00:21:12,550 --> 00:21:13,350
Okay.

211
00:23:15,510 --> 00:23:18,590
How many rooms do you have here?

212
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:20,590
Ten...

213
00:23:22,030 --> 00:23:23,400
Over ten.

214
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,880
You mean bedrooms, right?

215
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,440
Are there other rooms besides bedrooms?

216
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:32,200
There's a study, a wine cellar, a gym room,

217
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,240
and your favourite, a mini theatre.

218
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:39,070
You have a cinema room, and you don't watch films?

219
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:40,880
Unbelievable.

220
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:43,200
What?

221
00:23:52,030 --> 00:23:53,400
I forgot to prepare a birthday cake for you.

222
00:23:54,350 --> 00:23:55,240
It's okay.

223
00:23:57,030 --> 00:23:58,030
Happy birthday.

224
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:02,270
Thank you.

225
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:07,350
You really don't want anything as a gift?

226
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:12,070
Didn't you already give me the watch?

227
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:14,270
I'll just treat that as my gift.

228
00:24:16,550 --> 00:24:19,510
How about I renovate the mini theatre?

229
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:21,160
Then you can come over to watch films anytime.

230
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,830
You can watch whatever you want

231
00:24:23,030 --> 00:24:25,070
and enjoy brand-new equipment.

232
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,480
That sounds like too much trouble.

233
00:24:28,510 --> 00:24:30,880
I'd only be able to come in when you were home.

234
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,240
I'll give you a key.

235
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:37,030
And I'll keep a guest room for you.

236
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:38,720
You can stay up watching films as late as you want.

237
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:50,640
What?

238
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:52,240
Nothing.

239
00:24:53,270 --> 00:24:55,640
You just seem to be in a very good mood today.

240
00:24:58,590 --> 00:25:00,720
There's progress on the company's new project.

241
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,400
I found a new investor.

242
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,510
Which group?

243
00:25:06,720 --> 00:25:08,030
The So Group.

244
00:25:08,830 --> 00:25:10,880
They mainly focus on shipping.

245
00:25:11,030 --> 00:25:13,920
But Mr. So's daughter wants to enter the property industry.

246
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:16,000
I'm helping her negotiate

247
00:25:16,830 --> 00:25:19,240
for a seat on Tin Ping Group's board.

248
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,000
And the So Group's investment

249
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:23,550
in Tin Ping

250
00:25:23,550 --> 00:25:24,680
will be treated as her dowry.

251
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:28,680
Dowry?

252
00:25:29,270 --> 00:25:30,070
Yes.

253
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:33,000
Mr. So is very conservative when it comes to business.

254
00:25:33,070 --> 00:25:34,680
He only works with his own people.

255
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,240
Besides, once we're married,

256
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,640
she'll face less resistance from the board

257
00:25:38,830 --> 00:25:40,240
when she joins Tin Ping.

258
00:25:42,590 --> 00:25:45,640
Who is Ms. So going to marry?

259
00:25:46,030 --> 00:25:47,240
Me, of course.

260
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,240
Who else could it be?

261
00:25:51,270 --> 00:25:52,400
You're getting married?

262
00:25:53,070 --> 00:25:53,880
That's right.

263
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:01,880
You're marrying someone else?

264
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:04,030
It's just a marriage of convenience.

265
00:26:04,830 --> 00:26:07,240
She and I are only friends.

266
00:26:07,550 --> 00:26:09,400
Besides, she doesn't even like men.

267
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:12,750
You're going to

268
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,790
marry someone else?

269
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:19,920
Yes.

270
00:26:19,920 --> 00:26:20,830
What's the problem?

271
00:26:25,550 --> 00:26:26,400
What's the problem?

272
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:30,240
Fei Foon.

273
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:34,590
It'll be a marriage in name only.

274
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:36,240
Chloe and I have no feelings for each other.

275
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:37,680
We're just friends.

276
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:41,200
Chloe?

277
00:26:43,070 --> 00:26:44,200
If you have something to say, say it.

278
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:45,680
Don't keep repeating

279
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:47,240
everything I say like a parrot.

280
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:49,110
Why?

281
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:52,680
Why did you tell me?

282
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:54,640
You told me not to hide things from you.

283
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:56,440
Now that I've told you, you're upset.

284
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:00,110
Who suggested it?

285
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:01,110
Suggested what?

286
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:02,830
The marriage.

287
00:27:03,510 --> 00:27:05,070
We came up with the idea together.

288
00:27:08,070 --> 00:27:09,070
Who brought it up first?

289
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:12,240
She hinted at it. I made the proposal. Okay?

290
00:27:12,240 --> 00:27:13,920
Her father's been pressuring her to get married.

291
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,830
When you proposed,

292
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:17,920
did you stop for even a second

293
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,350
and think about how I'd feel

294
00:27:20,590 --> 00:27:22,000
if I found out?

295
00:27:24,030 --> 00:27:26,510
The marriage is fake.

296
00:27:26,830 --> 00:27:27,510
As soon as the project...

297
00:27:27,510 --> 00:27:28,510
So you didn't!

298
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:32,240
You're being unreasonable!

299
00:27:33,030 --> 00:27:33,510
It's fake.

300
00:27:33,510 --> 00:27:34,590
I said it's fake!

301
00:27:36,830 --> 00:27:38,350
I went through all this trouble

302
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:40,440
to bring this investment into the company.

303
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:42,000
Shouldn't you be happy for me?

304
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:43,720
Your company.

305
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:45,880
It's always about your company.

306
00:27:47,510 --> 00:27:49,720
Have you ever thought about us?

307
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:54,720
Thought about us?

308
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:57,110
How am I supposed to think about us?

309
00:27:58,790 --> 00:27:59,790
When I socialise with people,

310
00:28:00,240 --> 00:28:01,400
I have to bring a female companion.

311
00:28:01,790 --> 00:28:03,350
A man can only be kept at home.

312
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:05,310
Look at this ashtray.

313
00:28:05,830 --> 00:28:06,590
Look at it.

314
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:08,160
It's beautiful, isn't it?

315
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:10,240
But would you take it out with you?

316
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:23,880
I understand now.

317
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:31,270
Hey, Fei Foon.

318
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:35,830
I've seen Chloe in the financial pages.

319
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:38,030
She's very pretty.

320
00:28:42,590 --> 00:28:43,590
Congratulations

321
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:46,480
on finding such a beautiful partner.

322
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:52,310
Can you stop talking like that?

323
00:28:53,310 --> 00:28:54,030
Okay.

324
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:56,510
No problem.

325
00:28:59,030 --> 00:29:00,270
I have nothing else to ask.

326
00:29:08,030 --> 00:29:08,550
Fei Foon.

327
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:09,550
Okay.

328
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:10,720
Give me some more time.

329
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:12,350
Let me think of another way to secure the investment, okay?

330
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:15,550
What exactly are we to each other?

331
00:29:21,070 --> 00:29:21,960
I wish you

332
00:29:22,110 --> 00:29:23,270
and Tin Ping Group

333
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:25,070
all the best.

334
00:29:33,590 --> 00:29:36,400
Fei Foon, what do you want me to do?

335
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:39,480
Whatever you want.

336
00:30:07,260 --> 00:30:11,980
♪Loving you always comes with rumours and whispers♪

337
00:30:12,110 --> 00:30:13,400
You're pretty badly hurt.

338
00:30:14,010 --> 00:30:19,150
♪I hear you treat love like a circus act♪

339
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:21,980
♪You make me happy, then forget it all♪

340
00:30:23,310 --> 00:30:25,890
♪You admire me, then cast me aside♪

341
00:30:27,060 --> 00:30:34,160
♪Loving you means hating myself at the same time♪

342
00:30:36,780 --> 00:30:40,340
♪Like we're in love on the edge of a cliff♪

343
00:30:40,990 --> 00:30:44,250
♪How thrilling can it really be?♪

344
00:30:44,370 --> 00:30:50,580
♪I only win your love by fooling myself♪

345
00:30:51,150 --> 00:30:53,920
♪Love beneath a crumbling wall♪

346
00:30:54,570 --> 00:30:58,240
♪Brings far too much heartache♪

347
00:30:59,170 --> 00:31:02,020
♪I hate that I should♪

348
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:05,650
♪Walk away...♪

349
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:10,110
I bumped into Hui Loek To on the street.

350
00:31:10,110 --> 00:31:11,510
Then I invited him over to my place...

351
00:31:14,830 --> 00:31:19,970
♪In the end, I choose to love you blindly♪

352
00:31:20,730 --> 00:31:23,450
♪Maybe I deserve it♪

353
00:31:24,170 --> 00:31:26,810
♪Because I can't live without you♪

354
00:31:27,980 --> 00:31:33,990
♪Rumours do their best to turn black into white for you♪

355
00:31:34,110 --> 00:31:37,830
♪Falling in love with you on the edge of a cliff♪

356
00:31:38,460 --> 00:31:41,940
♪How thrilling can it really be?♪

357
00:31:42,030 --> 00:31:48,080
♪I only win your love by fooling myself♪

358
00:31:48,730 --> 00:31:51,280
♪Love beneath a crumbling wall♪

359
00:31:52,050 --> 00:31:56,160
♪Brings far too much heartache♪

360
00:31:56,350 --> 00:31:59,700
♪I hate that I should♪

361
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:03,800
♪Let go♪

362
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:11,370
♪If it's the wrong kind of love, I dare not admit it♪

363
00:32:11,660 --> 00:32:14,930
♪Cruelty is inevitable♪

364
00:32:15,140 --> 00:32:19,640
♪Tears are inevitable♪

365
00:33:15,030 --> 00:33:16,550
The public had never known

366
00:33:16,550 --> 00:33:18,720
that the two of you were a couple.

367
00:33:18,720 --> 00:33:20,270
So when you suddenly announced

368
00:33:20,270 --> 00:33:21,680
your engagement,

369
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:22,880
everyone was very surprised.

370
00:33:23,030 --> 00:33:24,720
Why did you choose this time

371
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:26,030
to make the announcement?

372
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:28,640
We always wanted to keep things low-key.

373
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:31,270
But recently, there have been many false rumours

374
00:33:31,270 --> 00:33:33,400
about Vincent and Tin Ping Group.

375
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:34,830
I was furious when I heard them.

376
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,640
So as his strongest supporter,

377
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:38,030
I wanted to stand by him

378
00:33:38,030 --> 00:33:39,350
at this time.

379
00:33:39,550 --> 00:33:40,880
I'm very lucky

380
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,270
to have Chloe's support.

381
00:33:42,830 --> 00:33:44,880
We've learned

382
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:47,590
that Chloe will be joining Tin Ping Group's board.

383
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:50,400
What changes will this bring to Tin Ping?

384
00:33:50,680 --> 00:33:51,400
Of course,

385
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:54,240
new people bring new approaches.

386
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:57,070
Going forward, the board will be able to make decisions

387
00:33:57,070 --> 00:33:58,590
more efficiently and clearly.

388
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,830
And with Chloe's investment,

389
00:34:01,070 --> 00:34:02,110
we'll have more flexibility

390
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:03,550
when acquiring land

391
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:05,240
and selecting contractors.

392
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:07,550
We'll face far fewer constraints.

393
00:34:08,230 --> 00:34:09,230
Thank you both for your time.

394
00:34:09,230 --> 00:34:11,110
That's all for today.

395
00:34:11,110 --> 00:34:14,230
Lastly, we'd like Mr. Hui to give Chloe a kiss.

396
00:34:14,230 --> 00:34:16,230
We'd like to take a few more photos.

397
00:34:18,070 --> 00:34:20,230
A kiss on the cheek is fine too.

398
00:34:29,030 --> 00:34:29,440
Okay.

399
00:34:29,440 --> 00:34:30,880
Please hold that pose a little longer.

400
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:38,630
Thank you, Mr. Hui.

401
00:34:38,670 --> 00:34:39,550
Thank you, Chloe.

402
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:46,070
Hello, Auntie, Terrance.

403
00:34:46,510 --> 00:34:47,400
Chloe,

404
00:34:47,440 --> 00:34:49,440
I haven't congratulated you and Vincent yet.

405
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:52,030
I'll send you a wedding gift later.

406
00:34:52,110 --> 00:34:53,070
Thank you, Auntie.

407
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:54,230
Don't mention it.

408
00:34:54,880 --> 00:34:57,590
From now on, please take good care of Vincent for me.

409
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:01,230
I've made a reservation in East Tsim Sha Tsui.

410
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:03,030
Let's have lunch together.

411
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:06,030
I'd like to get to know you properly.

412
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:07,590
I'm sorry, Auntie,

413
00:35:07,670 --> 00:35:09,590
but Terrance and I have a media interview scheduled

414
00:35:09,590 --> 00:35:11,840
to introduce Tin Ping Group's ESG development plans.

415
00:35:12,030 --> 00:35:13,670
I'm afraid we won't have time for lunch. Sorry.

416
00:35:14,510 --> 00:35:15,400
Silly child,

417
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:16,190
no need to apologise.

418
00:35:16,550 --> 00:35:17,880
Work comes first.

419
00:35:17,920 --> 00:35:19,000
You two should get going.

420
00:35:19,230 --> 00:35:20,670
- I'll get going, then.
- Mum, Loek To, goodbye.

421
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:21,110
Okay.

422
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:21,920
Goodbye.

423
00:35:27,550 --> 00:35:28,440
Congratulations

424
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:31,320
on marrying such a capable woman.

425
00:35:31,670 --> 00:35:33,510
New people bring new approaches.

426
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:36,920
Looks like your uncles and I have no choice but to hand over

427
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:37,760
power to you.

428
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:38,840
Don't worry.

429
00:35:39,230 --> 00:35:41,030
I won't put you in a difficult position.

430
00:35:41,590 --> 00:35:43,000
Do whatever you want.

431
00:35:43,190 --> 00:35:43,920
I have no objections.

432
00:35:54,670 --> 00:35:56,230
What's left on today's schedule?

433
00:35:56,670 --> 00:35:57,880
No more business arrangements.

434
00:35:58,230 --> 00:35:59,710
I'm ready to call it a day.

435
00:36:00,590 --> 00:36:01,840
Don't you have plans with anyone today?

436
00:36:03,360 --> 00:36:04,280
None of your business.

437
00:36:04,280 --> 00:36:05,510
If you're leaving, go ahead.

438
00:36:06,710 --> 00:36:07,710
I'll get going, then.

439
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:50,110
Thanks.

440
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:51,920
Officer Mok,

441
00:36:52,230 --> 00:36:53,110
are you in a bad mood?

442
00:37:00,110 --> 00:37:00,920
Drink.

443
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:03,440
Could I have another glass, please?

444
00:37:03,670 --> 00:37:04,440
Sure.

445
00:37:08,590 --> 00:37:10,190
Have you been troubled by something lately?

446
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:12,360
You've been looking down all day.

447
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:14,880
You could say I got dumped.

448
00:37:17,030 --> 00:37:18,440
Don't be upset over someone who hurt you.

449
00:37:20,070 --> 00:37:21,150
You're a wonderful guy.

450
00:37:21,190 --> 00:37:21,920
Anyone who hurts you

451
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,000
can't be a good person.

452
00:37:24,070 --> 00:37:24,880
You're right.

453
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:27,880
I knew he wasn't a good person.

454
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:30,440
Out with the old, in with the new.

455
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,400
Come on.

456
00:37:31,550 --> 00:37:32,590
I'll drink with you tonight.

457
00:37:32,710 --> 00:37:33,400
We won't leave until we're drunk.

458
00:37:33,510 --> 00:37:34,920
Drink until you completely forget him.

459
00:37:35,840 --> 00:37:36,230
Come on.

460
00:37:45,710 --> 00:37:47,440
But it's not that easy to forget someone.

461
00:37:48,590 --> 00:37:49,920
Am I supposed to pretend he never existed?

462
00:37:52,070 --> 00:37:52,710
What are you looking at?

463
00:37:52,710 --> 00:37:53,400
Drink.

464
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:54,880
You said it yourself.

465
00:37:55,230 --> 00:37:56,550
We won't leave until we're drunk.

466
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:57,440
Okay.

467
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:58,880
We won't leave until we're drunk.

468
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:03,590
Hello.

469
00:38:03,590 --> 00:38:04,320
Just the two of you?

470
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:04,710
Yes.

471
00:38:04,710 --> 00:38:05,440
Let's drink together.

472
00:38:05,590 --> 00:38:06,000
Sure.

473
00:38:06,030 --> 00:38:06,710
Come drink with us.

474
00:38:06,710 --> 00:38:07,440
Keep my boss company.

475
00:38:07,440 --> 00:38:08,480
He's in a bad mood.

476
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:10,320
Help me cheer him up.

477
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:11,960
Why do you look so miserable?

478
00:38:12,070 --> 00:38:13,000
Did you get dumped?

479
00:38:13,510 --> 00:38:14,880
Yeah. A man dumped me.

480
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:16,230
Don't bring that up anymore.

481
00:38:16,230 --> 00:38:17,030
Let's drink.

482
00:38:17,030 --> 00:38:17,550
Sure.

483
00:38:17,550 --> 00:38:18,670
Cheers.

484
00:38:20,070 --> 00:38:20,880
Cheers.

485
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:25,440
Don't let his gloomy look fool you.

486
00:38:25,550 --> 00:38:27,360
He's usually the most impressive one

487
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:28,670
on our team.

488
00:38:29,230 --> 00:38:30,670
Is he a good drinker?

489
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:32,030
Of course.

490
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:34,510
Today just happens to be your unlucky day.

491
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:36,670
He can drink a lot.

492
00:38:37,670 --> 00:38:39,230
Then let's order more drinks.

493
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:40,480
I'll pour you another one, boss.

494
00:38:41,230 --> 00:38:42,030
You guys chat first.

495
00:38:42,030 --> 00:38:42,880
Have some.

496
00:38:43,030 --> 00:38:44,110
Drink it yourself.

497
00:38:44,590 --> 00:38:45,840
You're no fun.

498
00:38:46,030 --> 00:38:47,070
What's your star sign?

499
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:49,320
My friend is a Cancer.

500
00:38:50,110 --> 00:38:51,000
A Cancer?

501
00:38:51,230 --> 00:38:51,710
Perfect.

502
00:38:51,710 --> 00:38:53,400
He likes Cancers the most.

503
00:38:53,510 --> 00:38:54,360
Girls with gentle personalities.

504
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:55,710
Don't let him fool you. He's just acting cool.

505
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:56,920
Boss, drink up.

506
00:38:57,710 --> 00:38:58,550
Come on.

507
00:38:58,590 --> 00:39:00,030
Have a drink with my friend.

508
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:01,230
Cheers.

509
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:02,510
Come on.

510
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:07,840
Officer Mok, hold on a little longer.

511
00:39:08,110 --> 00:39:08,920
Just a little longer.

512
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:14,880
We're almost there.

513
00:39:15,110 --> 00:39:16,320
Hang in there.

514
00:40:01,880 --> 00:40:02,670
Officer Mok,

515
00:40:03,550 --> 00:40:05,230
you always seem so sharp and capable,

516
00:40:06,030 --> 00:40:11,710
but when you're drunk, you're surprisingly weak and helpless.

517
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:15,840
You must have been born under a lucky star

518
00:40:17,590 --> 00:40:21,400
to shine so brightly wherever you go.

519
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:29,110
Don't blame me.

520
00:40:30,230 --> 00:40:32,030
You brought this upon yourself.

521
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:32,710
Yee,

522
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,230
I brought him back.

523
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:35,550
Hello, Officer Mok.

524
00:41:35,550 --> 00:41:36,190
I'm Joseph.

525
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:38,360
After finding out he was the one who killed you,

526
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:39,760
I started getting close to him

527
00:41:39,920 --> 00:41:41,030
and told K to make his move.

528
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:42,320
Watch out!

529
00:41:44,030 --> 00:41:45,440
Shall I give you a ride home?

530
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:46,760
Don't worry about me.

531
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,510
Just finish your work and go home.

532
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:51,110
You traitor!

533
00:41:54,710 --> 00:41:56,960
Too bad K ended up dead.

534
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:57,360
Call an ambulance.

535
00:41:57,360 --> 00:41:58,230
Yes, sir.

536
00:41:58,230 --> 00:42:01,110
I swore I'd avenge you.

537
00:42:01,590 --> 00:42:03,320
I've waited a long time for this day.

538
00:42:12,070 --> 00:42:13,230
Leung Yee was your brother?

539
00:42:14,110 --> 00:42:16,550
So you're the mole he planted in the police station.

540
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:17,960
While you were undercover,

541
00:42:18,550 --> 00:42:19,440
you could've just had him arrested.

542
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:20,360
Why did you have to get him killed?

543
00:42:20,550 --> 00:42:22,000
Who really got him killed?

544
00:42:22,760 --> 00:42:24,150
If Leung Yee hadn't been tipped off beforehand

545
00:42:24,190 --> 00:42:25,400
and disrupted the police operation,

546
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:26,400
how could he have died?

547
00:42:26,400 --> 00:42:27,400
Shut up!

548
00:42:54,670 --> 00:42:55,550
Sit,

549
00:42:55,550 --> 00:42:57,550
come back to the station with me and explain everything to Officer Chan.

550
00:42:57,670 --> 00:42:59,230
We'll work this out together.

551
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:00,880
Work this out?

552
00:43:01,110 --> 00:43:01,710
Officer Mok,

553
00:43:02,230 --> 00:43:03,590
do you really think I'm stupid?

554
00:43:05,110 --> 00:43:06,280
Sit, let go!

555
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:14,110
Even if I die,

556
00:43:14,590 --> 00:43:16,800
I'll make sure my death means something!

557
00:43:39,460 --> 00:43:44,500
[Episode 5]

558
00:43:44,590 --> 00:43:59,820
[This story is fictional. Any resemblance is entirely coincidental.]
